bodyguard-of-bits (0.14.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * BREAKING contract-fix bundle. The "teeth" originally planned for this
    version (container/nftables scoring deductions) stay deferred: they need
    a real container and a real cloud instance to calibrate, and guessing
    would violate the project's own rule.
  * scoring: the audit profile is now carried by ScoreEngine and applied
    inside apply(), the single choke point every check result passes
    through. Previously the caller had to invoke apply_profile() first, and
    only 2 of the 14 engine.apply() sites in bob/runner.py did — the 12
    hand-rolled always-on sections never applied it, leaving 8 shipped
    overrides in desktop.conf and workstation.conf silently dead. The most
    visible consequence: services.exposure.open_local stayed WARN on every
    profile, so a host running Samba restricted to the LAN by a UFW rule —
    the recommended configuration — could never return exit 0, although 0 is
    documented as "No issues detected" and the exit codes are a stable
    public API. BREAKING on desktop/workstation (warning_count drops); server
    is unchanged, it ships zero overrides by design.
  * output: colour is auto-detected. `bob > report.txt` and `bob | less` no
    longer contain ANSI escape codes; set FORCE_COLOR=1 for the old
    behaviour. supports_color() had existed all along, correct and called
    from nowhere. Resolution order: --no-color, then NO_COLOR, then
    FORCE_COLOR, then isatty(). print_help hardcoded its own bold escape, so
    `bob --no-color --help` printed bold anyway — it now goes through the
    same decision, with a guard forbidding literal escapes in bob/cli.py.
  * help: the --no-color line said "NO_COLOR= also work", which reads either
    as the assignment or as the empty value — and the empty value is exactly
    the case that does not disable colour. Replaced by an explicit entry for
    NO_COLOR and FORCE_COLOR.
  * lint: B904 and B905, deferred through v0.13.x because they change
    runtime behaviour, are addressed; .ruff.toml now ignores nothing.
  * packaging: 5 debian and 3 rpm changelog entries named the wrong weekday
    (lintian debian-changelog-has-wrong-day-of-week); all 46 entries in each
    file are now correct, with a guard that recomputes the day from the date.

