bodyguard-of-bits (0.13.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * First v0.13.x release — scope expansion: two new INFO-only hardening
    checks. BOB's first real coverage growth after the long internal-hardening
    cycle. Additive, non-BREAKING, no score change.
  * Service hardening (systemd-analyze security) — new section
    systemd_hardening. Runs `systemd-analyze security --json=short` scoped to
    running service units; surfaces a summary (counts by predicate UNSAFE /
    EXPOSED / OK), the least-hardened running services, and a pointer to
    `systemd-analyze security <unit>`. No deduction by design: most units ship
    unhardened by default (systemd's own docs call the exposure score a
    relative guide, not a vulnerability verdict), so deducting would be noise
    and would over-claim. A narrow admin-authored-unit deduction is deferred
    to real-world signal. Field-tested live EN+FR.
  * Container security posture — new section container_security, suppressed on
    a normal host and run only inside a container. Reads the container's own
    isolation from offline kernel interfaces: capability bounding set
    (/proc/self/status CapBnd → privileged / CAP_SYS_ADMIN detection +
    dangerous-cap list), seccomp mode, user-namespace mapping
    (/proc/self/uid_map), writable rootfs (/proc/mounts). Detection via
    systemd-detect-virt, /.dockerenv, /run/.containerenv, /proc/1/cgroup.
    INFO-only; a privileged-container WARN deduction is a fast-follow once it
    can accrue runtime signal. Validated against real kernel /proc data inside
    Linux user namespaces (unshare): privileged + non-privileged + the
    userns-suppresses-host-root-warning branch, EN+FR.
  * Section count 35 -> 36.
  * Tests 6442 -> 6461 (+19: 7 systemd + 12 container). 0 regression.
  * End-of-life: v0.12.x is now declared EOL (latest-minor-line-only policy);
    v0.8.x-v0.11.x likewise EOL; v0.13.x is the only supported line. v0.7.x /
    v0.6.x remain EOL. SECURITY.md / SECURITY_FR.md updated.
  * Upgrade: pipx upgrade bodyguard-of-bits. Fully backwards-compatible — two
    INFO-only sections added; no existing field, score, or exit code changed.

