bodyguard-of-bits (0.12.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Planned BREAKING UX bundle (F1/F2/F4/F6/F9) from the deep bilingual live
    test of v0.11.x — the five findings that could not ride a patch because
    each changes a contract, an exit code, or the score.
  * F1 (BREAKING, score model) — "10/10 means a flawless audit". The headline
    score is the mean of the active domain scores; rounding that average up
    could erase a real deduction (one pending firmware update averaged to
    10/10 while the summary still said "Action required"). When ANY deduction
    exists the headline is now capped at 9/10 — a perfect 10 is reserved for
    an audit with nothing to fix. --breakdown shows the average -> cap as two
    explicit steps, and the JSON "score" reflects the capped value.
  * F2 (presentation) — the summary per-item bullet now reflects the finding's
    SEVERITY (warn / alert) to match the body. Pre-fix a WARN-level action
    item showed the alert symbol in the summary but the warn symbol in the
    body; the section header still groups by nature.
  * F4 (BREAKING, exit code) — "bob --explain <unknown-key>" now exits 3
    instead of 0, so scripts can distinguish "explained" from "no such key",
    and prints a difflib "did you mean" fuzzy suggestion for typos.
  * F6 — --check / --skip token validation now runs BEFORE the root gate, so
    "bob --check=typo" without sudo reports the unknown token instead of
    first demanding root.
  * F9 (BREAKING, JSON schema v2 -> v3) — the integer count keys "alerts" and
    "warnings" are renamed "alert_count" / "warning_count" for symmetry with
    "info_count" (a consumer iterating data["alerts"] expecting a list got an
    int). A key rename is breaking, so schema_version bumps v2 -> v3 following
    the clean-cut pattern (v2 retired exactly as v1 was in v0.9.0; only the
    current major is emitted, no legacy builders kept). The webhook generic
    payload keeps alerts/warnings — it has no info_count and is its own
    separate contract.
  * Test isolation — the watch score-bar tests now force monochrome output
    explicitly instead of relying on a leaked global colour state.
  * Tests 6381 -> 6401 (+20). 0 regression.

