bodyguard-of-bits (0.11.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Two minors from the post-v0.11.0 whole-tool deep hardening audit
    (0 critical + 0 important + 2 minor — a clean pass after 19 audits;
    cmd construction, atomic-write, HTML escaping, literal-key contracts
    all verified clean).
  * M-1 — i18n must not crash on a malformed locale template.
    bob/i18n.py::t() caught only KeyError from str.format(). A malformed
    template (unbalanced brace -> ValueError, positional {0} field ->
    IndexError) would propagate uncaught and crash the audit for the
    affected locale. t() now degrades to the raw template on
    (KeyError, IndexError, ValueError); try_t() gains the
    IndexError/ValueError guard while keeping its intentional KeyError
    propagation (a forgotten kwarg is a caller error, distinct from a
    corrupt template). The locale linter gains TestTemplateWellFormed,
    which rejects unbalanced braces and positional fields in en.json /
    fr.json at CI time so a malformed string can never ship. Current
    locales are clean; this closes a crash-on-future-edit class
    consistent with the bracketed-fallback contract.
  * M-2 — --test-webhook now honors --offline. --offline is a global
    no-egress guard for air-gapped environments. The audit-time webhook
    path already gated on `not config.offline`, but the explicit
    --test-webhook command did not, so `bob --test-webhook --offline`
    still issued a POST. The offline guard now wins: the test is skipped
    cleanly with a clear stderr notice and EXIT_OK, before any URL
    resolution or network import. New locale key
    cli.test_webhook.offline_skipped (EN+FR).
  * Plus three trivially-safe polish fixes from the post-v0.11.0
    functional / perceived-quality (UX) audit — the no-contract-change
    subset; the score-model + presentation + exit-code + root-gate items
    (F1/F2/F4/F6) are deferred to the planned v0.12.0 bundle.
  * F3 — fwupd device-name parsing leaked connector junk. Under the
    default LC_ALL=C, `fwupdmgr get-updates` renders its device tree
    connectors as `?`, breaking tree detection; the parser fell to flat
    mode and surfaced `?` / `??UEFI dbx:` / the container header as
    device names (observed live: "ASUSTeK ... , ?, ??UEFI dbx:"). Now
    runs fwupd under C.UTF-8 (new _C_UTF8_LOCALE_ENV) so the tree renders
    correctly, plus a parser guard rejecting names not starting with an
    alphanumeric. Live result is now the clean "1 pending firmware
    update(s): UEFI dbx".
  * F5 — the unknown-key explain hint wrongly said "Run 'sudo bob
    --explain list'"; `--explain list` needs no sudo. Dropped it (EN+FR).
  * F7 — a protocol-unspecified UFW orphan rule displayed a bare port
    ("57621") next to proto-qualified siblings ("41681/tcp"). Now shows
    "57621/tcp+udp" (UFW applies it to both); the delete command keeps
    the bare port.
  * Plus a documentation accuracy pass (DOC-A...G): a full doc audit
    cross-checking every prose doc + man page + CLI help against the
    real code, folding in the no-risk corrections. --json-v1 (retired
    v0.9.0) removed from TUTORIAL / README_TECH / SECURITY where it was
    still shown as a usable flag; the workstation profile reconciled to
    first-class business-tier (README called it an alias, man said
    "shipped but not consumed" — both described the pre-v0.8.1
    behaviour) and added to the --help profile line + --profile error
    message where it was omitted; stale EXPLAIN_KEYS counts (116 / 168)
