    for retrait in v0.7.0 + v0.8.0 SECURITY.md. Plugins always execute
    in the spawn'd subprocess sandbox; setting the env var has no effect.
    The flashy stderr WARNING + CRITICAL log machinery removed alongside.
  * Cleanup — EXPLAIN_KEY_ALIASES retired (D-3). The v0.5.5 alias
    (services_state.service_inactive → enabled_inactive, became
    services_health.* after the D-1 rename) was a bridge over a
    source-side drift; v0.9.0 resolves the drift at the source (renamed
    the EXPLAIN_KEYS entry to .service_inactive to match what
    services_state.py emits) and clears the alias dict + removes the
    one-shot deprecation warning machinery added in v0.8.2.
  * Internal — _ALL_SECTIONS + _ALWAYS_ON_SECTIONS fusion (D-2). New
    _SECTIONS: tuple[_Section(name, always_on), ...] is the single
    source of truth; the two legacy tuples are derived views built once
    at import time for back-compat. External consumers (bob/__main__.py
    + tests) keep using the legacy names unchanged.
  * NEW — --diff [PATH] cross-machine compare (F-2). The --diff flag now
    optionally takes a baseline file path; with the path form, --diff
    loads the file in strict mode (missing/broken/v1-schema = CLI error)
    instead of the silent v0.8.x "no baseline yet" fallback. Baselines
    now record the source hostname; cross-machine compare surfaces an
    INFO notice with recorded vs current hostnames. Bare --diff / -D
    keeps the v0.8.x local-baseline behaviour.
  * Bug fix — bash completion "bob --check=<TAB><TAB>" without sudo
    returned zero candidates because some bash versions place the cursor
    on the literal "=" token (cur="=" prev="--check"); the completion
    function now normalises cur="=" → cur="" before the prefix-match
    branches, restoring TAB×2 list display under non-sudo invocations.
    Companion to the v0.8.2 sudo-dispatcher walk-back guard.
  * Tests 6246 (v0.8.4) → 6210 (v0.9.0). Net -36: -53 v1 baseline +
    deprecation-warning tests retired, +17 new F-2 tests.

