bodyguard-of-bits (0.8.3-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=high

  * HOTFIX: v0.8.2 audit path crashed with UnboundLocalError on every
    non --test-webhook invocation. Root cause: the v0.8.2 --test-webhook
    handler did `from bob.config import UserConfig` inside main(). Python's
    local-scope analyzer treated UserConfig as a function-local name for
    the entire body, so line 298 (audit path) raised
    `UnboundLocalError: cannot access local variable 'UserConfig'` on
    every regular `bob` invocation that didn't enter the --test-webhook
    branch. The same shadowing pattern existed for `os` and `traceback`
    inside the top-level except handler.
  * Fix: removed the redundant local imports of UserConfig + os; promoted
    `traceback` to a module-scope import. The module-level `from
    bob.config import UserConfig` (line 26) is now the single binding.
  * Regression guard: `tests/test_v083_main_scope_guard.py` (2 tests)
    statically asserts main() does not shadow any name imported at module
    scope. A future contributor who adds another defensive re-import
    inside main() fails this test before the audit path crashes for
    users.
  * v0.8.2 marked broken on PyPI; users should upgrade to v0.8.3
    immediately.
