bodyguard-of-bits (0.5.2-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Refactor v0.5.x Phase 3 (audit findings #4 + #3). Two pure
    structural refactors; zero behaviour change; 4538/4538 tests
    unchanged.
  * #4 — new _BadDirective frozen dataclass + _BAD_DIRECTIVES table
    + _apply_bad_directive() helper in bob/checks/ssh.py. Migrates
    8 uniform sshd_config directives (PermitEmptyPasswords,
    X11Forwarding, IgnoreRhosts, HostbasedAuthentication,
    PermitUserEnvironment, StrictModes, AllowTcpForwarding,
    PubkeyAuthentication) from a cascade of if-blocks to a
    declarative table + loop. _check_sshd_config body shrinks
    ~180 → ~50 LoC. Two predicate styles: bad_values tuple (most
    directives) and safe_values tuple (AllowTcpForwarding only,
    where "local" is acceptable). __post_init__ catches malformed
    entries at module load.
  * Sites kept imperative (don't fit the table): PermitRootLogin
    (4-way branch), PasswordAuthentication (depends on ssh_exposed),
    MaxAuthTries (integer threshold), LoginGraceTime (INFO-only),
    AllowUsers/AllowGroups, Match block, weak ciphers/macs/kex
