  * #7 — new is_unit_active() / is_unit_enabled() helpers in
    bob.checks._run; migrates the repeated
    `_run("systemctl", "is-active", X).strip() == "active"` idiom
    at 9 sites (auditd, fail2ban, clamav, ntp, ddns, updates, ssh,
    backup, log_rotation). Defensive .lower() added centrally to
    guard against non-canonical distro output.
    services._detect_single_unit_state keeps its richer state machine
    per audit recommendation.
  * #2 — new bob.output.print_titled_box(title, width=62); migrates
    4 sites (3x cron.py, 1x manage_logs.py). Closes a --no-color
    leak: those 4 sites previously bypassed _c by inlining
    \\033[1;34m literals, so --no-color did not strip the box
    colours.
  * #10 — new bob.report.Report typing.Protocol (PEP 544). Captures
    the shared write-method contract between AuditReport, NullReport,
    and MarkdownReport. runner.run_checks now type-hints
    `report: Report`. No @runtime_checkable — static typing only,
    zero overhead.
  * #11 — new emit_section() + emit_group() closures in
    runner.run_checks. Collapses the 3-line
    `if not config.quiet: print_section(t(...)); report.write_section(t(...))`
    motif into 1-line calls at 20 sites (5 group + 15 section
    headers). _sec() itself uses emit_section internally. Net
    runner.py: -28 lines.
  * #15a — new tests/test_domain_scores_mapping_complete.py (+4
    tests). AST-scan of bob/checks/*.py for every literal key="X.Y";
    asserts each prefix is either mapped in _PREFIX_TO_DOMAIN or
    whitelisted in _CATCH_ALL_BY_DESIGN with a justification. Guards
    the firewall catch-all from silent future drift.
  * Cron coverage pass (preliminary for Phase 5): +35 tests across
    5 new classes covering pure helpers
    (_validate_cron_field, _validate_custom_cron, build_script_content,
    apply_cron_schedule, apply_cron_email). Includes legacy
    NOTIFY_EMAIL= (no S) regex-parity coverage.
  * Latent bug fixed (surfaced by the new cron tests):
    apply_cron_schedule() referenced _os.open / _os.fdopen /
    _os.O_* — but _os is only locally aliased in three OTHER
    functions in cron.py, never at module level. The v0.4.8
    cron-deduplication extraction missed the rename. The helper had
    been silently dead since v0.4.8 ship — only the curses TUI wired
    it, and that path is not exercised by automated tests. Fix:
    `_os` -> `os` on 3 references / 2 lines.
  * Monitoring list (release-watch): two APIs added without immediate
    consumers — is_unit_enabled() (mirror of is_unit_active),
    print_titled_box() width parameter (never overridden at any call
    site). Tracked for review in v0.5.1-v0.5.4.
  * 4499 -> 4538 tests (+39: +4 mapping, +35 cron). Full suite
    passes in 7.77s on Python 3.12 / Linux Mint 22.3.

