bodyguard-of-bits (0.4.8-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Code-hardening release — sub-agent code-review pass 4 (4 important
    + 5 minor + 3 suggestion findings) plus deep pyproject.toml audit
    (6 packaging hardening fixes). No behaviour change in the audit
    pipeline; the JSON schema_version="1" contract, the 7 score
    domains, the 116 EXPLAIN_KEYS, and the 34 filterable sections are
    all preserved.
  * I4 (important): bob.report.Reporter and bob.manage_logs now call
    chown_to_sudo_user() on file/directory creation. When bob is
    invoked via sudo, the report file and the log directory tree are
    now owned by the invoking user instead of root — fixes a
    real-world ergonomic regression where users could not delete or
    edit their own audit artefacts without re-elevating.
  * I1-I3 + M4-M5 (important + minor): removed dead dataclass fields
    that were assigned but never read. Affected fields:
    ssh.config_source_files, firewall.ipv4_rules_count and
    firewall.ipv6_rules_count, samba.min_protocol, clamav.db_path,
    clamav.last_scan_log_path, secure_boot.method. Constructor
    arguments and intermediate parsing dropped accordingly.
  * M1 (minor): added _C_LOCALE_ENV (LC_ALL=C, LANG=C, LANGUAGE="")
    to 3 remaining subprocess.check_output sites in checks/desktop_apps.py
    and checks/smtp.py for consistency with the rest of the codebase.
  * M3 (minor): replaced the 12-line subprocess.run-based
    log_rotation._service_active helper with a 1-line call to the
    shared _run() helper (bob.checks._run). Same behaviour, less code.
  * M2 + S2 (minor + suggestion): extracted cron-entry mutation logic
    (schedule string + NOTIFY_EMAIL variable) into public helpers
    apply_cron_schedule() and apply_cron_email() in bob.cron. The TUI
    cron module now imports those helpers instead of duplicating the
    parsing logic. Preserves the legacy NOTIFY_EMAILS regex for
    backward parity.
  * S1 (suggestion): added a clarifying docstring to
    checks/auth_log.py explaining why the 90-day window is hardcoded
    and how it relates to the --log-days CLI flag.
  * S3 (suggestion): promoted bob.output._SCORE_BAR_WIDTH to a public
    SCORE_BAR_WIDTH constant; bob.breakdown and bob.domain_scores now
    import it instead of duplicating the literal value 10.
  * pyproject.toml hardening (v0.4.8): setuptools>=77 minimum
    (PEP 639 compliance + license metadata), wheel removed from
    build-system.requires (auto-resolved), authors and maintainers
    canonicalised to cedricclauzel@mailo.com, Development Status ::
    5 - Production/Stable classifier, explicit empty dependencies = []
    list, optional [project.optional-dependencies] for geoip2,
    [tool.setuptools.packages.find] restricted to bob/bob.checks/bob.tui.
  * 4499 tests (was 4500). The single removed test
    (tests/test_secure_boot.py::test_default_method_is_none) asserted
    a default value for the now-deleted method field, making it
    structurally meaningless. All other tests pass unchanged.

