    scores, and --manage-logs history now share a single coloured
    rendering via bob.output.score_bar() — green (score >= 8),
    yellow (5-7), red (0-4). Matches the existing disk partition
    bars in display._disk_bar. Affects display only; --no-color
    continues to neutralise the colours.
  * Bash completion (bob/data/bob.bash-completion) comprehensive
    overhaul. Critical fix: --check=, --skip=, --min-level=,
    --format=, --profile=, --lang=, --target=, --webhook-format=,
    --output= TAB-completions of values were all silently failing
    because the function read ${COMP_WORDS[COMP_CWORD]} which
    returns "=" when bash splits on the default COMP_WORDBREAKS.
    Fix: use the bash-completion positional-argument convention
    ($2 / $3) which provides the clean current word stripped of
    the '=' word-break prefix. Also: function renamed _ufw_audit
    -> _bob (legacy name from before the project rename); dead
    code removed (_ufw_audit_install for install.sh which no
    longer exists); section list factored and made to match
    `bob --check=list` exactly (was missing iptables_nft, samba,
    desktop_apps); long-options list now matches cli.py exactly
    (added --check=, --skip=, --output-dir=, --breakdown,
    --no-colour); short-options gained -B (--breakdown).
  * CI: .github/workflows/publish.yml gains a 4th job
    "github-release" that runs after PyPI publish succeeds. It
    extracts the release title from CHANGELOG.md table row, body
    from DOCUMENTS/CHANGELOG_FULL.md section, creates the GitHub
    release via softprops/action-gh-release@v2 with the wheel and
    sdist as attached assets, marks as latest. Removes the
    manual `gh release create` step.
  * 4500 tests (unchanged from v0.4.6). 3 tests in
    tests/test_breakdown.py::TestBar adapted to strip ANSI escape
    sequences before asserting visible bar content.

