bodyguard-of-bits (0.4.6-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Terrain test pass v0.4.5 fixes (2 reproducible bugs across 13 audits
    on 6 distinct systems, including production hardware).
  * Bug 1: bob/checks/kernel_modules.py — dpkg-query did not filter on
    'ii' state, so kernels left in 'rc' state after `apt remove` (without
    --purge) were still listed as installed. Now uses
    ${db:Status-Abbrev}|${Package} and keeps only lines whose 2nd char
    is 'i' (covers 'ii' and 'hi'; excludes 'rc', 'pn', 'un', 'iU').
  * Bug 2: bob/domain_scores.py::active_domains_from_engine() — scoring
    inversion after remediation. The actionable filter widened from
    (WARN, ALERT) to (OK, WARN, ALERT), so a domain that goes clean
    (only `updates.ok` left) stays at 10/10 in the global average
    instead of disappearing from the denominator. INFO-only domains
    remain hidden by design.
  * 4500 tests (+11 vs v0.4.5).
  * Multi-distro integration CI (additive): GitHub Actions matrix runs
    BOB inside containers of Debian 12/13, Ubuntu 22.04/24.04/25.04,
    Kali Rolling, Fedora 41 on every push/PR to main.

